Subject: [PATCH] cri: preserve pod MCS categories for container type-only overrides

When a nonprivileged container specifies only a SELinux type, use the pod
sandbox's recorded level instead of allocating independent categories.
Explicit levels, privileged containers, and user/role overrides retain
their existing behavior.

Use the shared label store for temporary container-creation references and
persist the sandbox process label so recovery preserves category ownership.
Include option-resolution and shared-reservation regression tests.

